From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:32:24 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Enable the SD card reader

The SDXC slot of the MacBook Pro (14-inch, M4) is a Genesys Logic GL9755
on internal PCIe port 2. From the J604 Apple device tree (26B123 runtime
capture):

  /arm-io/apcie/pci-bridge2   apcie-port 2, function-perst GPIO 165,
                              function-clkreq GPIO 162,
                              dart_* functions on /arm-io/dart-apcie2
  .../pcie-sdreader           pci17a0,9755 (rev 2) as enumerated by
                              macOS, function-sd_pwr_en =
                              pKW4(gP19, 0)
  /arm-io/dart-apcie2         0x492000000, AIC 1250

This is the layout every other Apple SD reader in this tree has (t600x
J314/J316 and J375, t603x J514/J516, t8122 J504): the port's power enable
is an ordinary SMC GPIO, which pcie-apple drives through pwren-gpios
before it trains the link, and a GL9755 node below the port. Here that is
SMC GPIO 0x19 (gP19); its pKW4 template is 0, unlike the radio's gP13
(0x800000), so it is a plain gpio-macsmc output. The root port's PERST#
(GPIO 165) and the port DART (0xc000 window, AIC 1250) are already in
t8132.dtsi.

Port 1 has no root port on this machine, so Linux gives port 2 bus 2
(00:02.0, secondary bus 2, measured with this port disabled). Map
requester ID 0x200 to stream 1 of the port 2 DART and fix the bus range,
as the J773g does for its port 2.

sdhci-pci binds the GL9755 by its PCI ID (MMC_SDHCI_PCI includes the
GL9755 support). cd-inverted and wp-inverted follow the other Apple
boards; sdhci-pci reads neither, the controller reports card detect and
write protect itself.

Loader dependency: the m1n1 T8132 PCIe handoff (pcie_fdt.c) prepares
every enabled port that has pwren-gpios and accepts only the radio rail
gP13. With m1n1 as it is, this port makes pcie_prepare_fdt() fail, and
kboot then disables the whole PCIe controller, Wi-Fi and Bluetooth
included. m1n1 has to leave rails other than the radio's to the OS before
this change can ship.

TO-VERIFY: a J604 boot with this device tree and that m1n1; a card in the
slot.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index 2a2e68d88e..ba972a558f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -278,7 +278,7 @@
  * Internal PCIe port 0: the Wi-Fi/Bluetooth module (BCM4388, Apple module
  * "guam"). m1n1 powers it through the same SMC action as pwren-gpios and
  * fills in the addresses, antenna SKU and calibration below. Port 1 is not
- * wired; port 2 (the SD card reader) stays off.
+ * wired. Port 2 is the SD card reader (below).
  */
 
 &pcie0_dart {
@@ -286,7 +286,8 @@
 };
 
 &pcie0 {
-	iommu-map = <0x100 &pcie0_dart 1 1>;
+	iommu-map = <0x100 &pcie0_dart 1 1>,
+		    <0x200 &pcie2_dart 1 1>;
 	status = "okay"; /* DTV-PCIE-1, DTV-PCIE-2 */
 };
 
@@ -313,6 +314,30 @@
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * Internal PCIe port 2: the SD card reader (Genesys Logic GL9755, ADT
+ * /arm-io/apcie/pci-bridge2/pcie-sdreader). Its power is the SMC GPIO gP19
+ * (function-sd_pwr_en, a plain pKW4 output), which pcie-apple switches on
+ * through pwren-gpios before it trains the link. Port 1 has no root port,
+ * so this port's secondary bus is 2.
+ */
+&pcie2_dart {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&pcie0_port2 {
+	pwren-gpios = <&smc_gpio 0x19 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+	bus-range = <2 2>;
+	status = "okay";
+
+	sdhci0: mmc@0,0 {
+		compatible = "pci17a0,9755";
+		reg = <0x20000 0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0>;
+		cd-inverted;
+		wp-inverted;
+	};
+};
+
 &mtp {
 	status = "okay"; /* DTV-MTP-3..5 */
 };
